 "purpose": "Builds the avatar: a 16x16 pixel face from layered parts, and the small reactions of the practice buddy.",
 "details": "The parts (shapes, colours, eyes, ears, nose, mouth expressions, hair, hats, accessories) are pixel-art data in inhoud/avatar/onderdelen.json; this module composes them into a raster of '#rrggbb' or None (transparent) that the terminal draws with half-block characters (terminal/avatar.py). An expression (happy, thinking, ...) picks the mouth and sometimes the eyes so the avatar reacts. It also holds the praise texts, the short 'psst' tips per diagnosis code and the text faces used when there is no room for pixels.",
 "module_docstring": "De avatar: een blokje van 16x16 pixels, samengesteld uit lagen (vorm, oren, ogen, neus, mond, haar, hoed, accessoire). Geeft gewone kleurdata terug; de terminal (of later een GUI) tekent ze.",
